The BIS January 2019 standard (d457, page 24) defines how to compute GIRR curvature sensitivities under SA   and  it is matching how  currently is being implemented

 The core assumption  is that   curvature is the incremental non-linearity effect  above delta effect. 
SO we that we need just to extract/capture the  Curvature residual  we  strip out what delta already explained:

a full reprice under a large shock contains both the linear (delta) effect and the non-linear (curvature) effect combined. Curvature is just the leftover once you strip out what delta already explained:

   CVR = [V_up or V_down − V_base] − [sum of delta sensitivities across all tenors × RW]

The repricing uses a parallel shift of the entire par curve — up and down — not tenor-by-tenor. 

Reference: https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d457.pdf — page 24.
